# Cargo never reads this file. It is not a `.gitignore` for packaging, it is not
# consulted by `cargo package`, and no version of Cargo has ever supported it.
#
# It used to hold 250 lines mirroring `.gitignore` byte for byte, and those lines
# were published *inside* the crate — protection that protected nothing, sitting
# in the tarball as if it were policy. The next maintainer to add a rule here
# would have believed the package was covered.
#
# Packaging is governed by `include` in Cargo.toml, which is an allowlist:
# nothing enters the crate unless it is named there or matched by one of its
# directory globs. See the comment above that field for why it is not `exclude`.
#
# `tests/policy/packaging.rs` fails the suite if any rule returns to this file.
